---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MakeFashion Edu"
  description="We're the educational heart of the MakeFashion program, driven by creativity and innovation. Students weave together fashion and technology, crafting outfits while mastering design thinking and hands-on building."
>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       HERO
       ===================================================================== -->
  <section class="hero" aria-label="MakeFashion Edu">
    <img
      class="hero__bg"
      src="/images/2024/01/IMG_8823-scaled.jpg"
      alt="MakeFashion Edu students on the runway"
    />
    <div class="container hero__content">
      <h1>MakeFashion Edu</h1>
      <p class="hero__tagline">
        We're the educational heart of the MakeFashion program, driven by creativity
        and innovation.
      </p>
      <a href="https://www.steamhead.space/contact-us/" class="btn btn--primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Get Involved
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       INTRODUCTION
       ===================================================================== -->
  <section class="section" aria-label="About MakeFashion Edu">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <h2>About the Program</h2>
          <hr class="accent-rule" />
          <p>
            Our students weave together fashion and technology, crafting outfits from
            scratch while mastering design thinking, technical skills, and hands-on
            building. Join us on this journey of self-expression and community
            storytelling!
          </p>
          <p>
            MakeFashion Edu is an international non-profit working to promote learning
            through fashion and tech. Through hosting workshops, reach-out and push-in
            activities, and larger events, MakeFashion Edu sees providing access for
            young designers to industry and project-based learning as one way to pull
            local communities together.
          </p>
          <p>
            MakeFashion Edu provides a year-round suite of education programs and
            support for K–12 educators and students, and has proven to be a powerful
            entry point — especially for girls who are hesitant to engage with science
            and technology subjects.
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          src="/images/2021/03/s3.jpeg"
          alt="MakeFashion Edu student showcasing wearable tech"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       BANNER
       ===================================================================== -->
  <img
    class="banner-img"
    src="/images/2024/01/hr-nologo-1170467-scaled.jpg"
    alt="MakeFashion Edu community"
  />

  <!-- =====================================================================
       THE RUNWAY
       ===================================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--alt" aria-label="The Runway">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="two-col two-col--reverse">
        <img
          src="/images/2024/02/shenzhen2019_02.jpg"
          alt="MakeFashion Edu runway show in Shenzhen 2019"
        />
        <div>
          <h2>The Runway</h2>
          <hr class="accent-rule" />
          <p>
            MakeFashion Edu runways are held in public spaces, and are the culminating
            event that students work towards throughout the program.
          </p>
          <p>
            The critical skills and processes all occur in the months leading up to the
            runway event, but the public display is a huge factor in motivating everyone
            and ensuring accountability to a large audience.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       THE CLASSES
       ===================================================================== -->
  <section class="section" aria-label="The Classes">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <h2>The Classes</h2>
          <hr class="accent-rule" />
          <p>
            MakeFashion Edu classes are held in schools or education centers around
            the world.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ideally lasting an entire semester, these classes focus on design,
            storytelling, and use technology as a secondary objective. These experiences
            excel at bringing students who do not self-identify as engineers toward using
            technology to complete projects they find compelling.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="img-pair">
          <img
            src="/images/2024/01/mfedu_landing02.png"
            alt="MakeFashion Edu classroom activity"
          />
          <img
            src="/images/2024/01/mfedu_landing03.png"
            alt="Students presenting their MakeFashion projects"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       THE BOOKS
       ===================================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--alt" aria-label="The Books">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="two-col two-col--reverse">
        <img
          src="/images/2024/02/Screenshot-2024-02-22-at-10.53.10.png"
          alt="MakeFashion Edu publication"
        />
        <div>
          <h2>The Books</h2>
          <hr class="accent-rule" />
          <p>
            Get inspired by the MakeFashion Edu final projects of each season.
          </p>
          <p>
            These books contain gallery shots, materials used, and the narrative stories
            behind each project — capturing the creativity and hard work of our students
            in a lasting publication.
          </p>
          <a href="/shop/" class="btn btn--primary mt-md">Browse Publications</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       PHOTO FROM CLASS
       ===================================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--dark" aria-label="Program highlights">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <h2>A Powerful Entry Point</h2>
          <hr class="accent-rule" />
          <p>
            MakeFashion Edu has proven to be a powerful entry point for students of all
            perspectives and backgrounds — but especially for girls who are hesitant to
            engage with science and technology subjects.
          </p>
          <p>
            By grounding technology in self-expression and storytelling, the program
            makes engineering feel relevant and accessible to learners who might otherwise
            opt out of STEAM pathways.
          </p>
          <a href="https://www.steamhead.space/contact-us/" class="btn btn--outline mt-md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Bring MFEdu to Your School
          </a>
        </div>
        <img
          src="/images/2024/01/IMG_1041.jpg"
          alt="MakeFashion Edu student at work"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .img-pair {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
